    "hihat-lofi": {
      "id": "hihat-lofi",
      "origin": "hihat-lofi",
      "name": "Lo-Fi Hi-Hat",
      "category": "modular",
      "notes": "REBUILT 2026-09-28 as a MODAL PLATE with collision RATTLE (see\ngen_cymbal_modal in modular_stages.c) against a user-supplied acoustic\nclosed hi-hat. The legacy variant-0 voice was six square oscillators plus\nflat white noise: measured on the reference it was all wrong in the way that\nreads \"electronic\" — spectral flatness 0.006 (six tones) where the real hat\nis 0.29 (noise-like), energy flat to 20 kHz where the real hat centres on\n8-12 kHz and rolls off above 14 kHz, and a peak at 0.4 ms where the real hat\nswells over ~8 ms and holds a CHATTERING ~40 ms plateau before it decays.\n\nThat plateau is the physics of a hi-hat (Sekiguchi \u0026 Samejima 2023): two\ncymbals clamped together, the top one re-colliding with the bottom after the\nstick hit. The voice models it directly — the plate's impulse response\nre-struck by a decaying Poisson train of collision impulses — so the noise\nis the plate itself rattling, not a noise generator.\n\nFITTED on the real C render: 1/3-octave x time energy map (1-16 kHz, 0-320\nms) + the 2 ms envelope over the first 60 ms + spectral flatness, minimized\nby coordinate descent. Score 4.1 against 32 for the legacy voice on the same\nmeasure. Units: env_tail / env_fast Np/s, *_f Hz, *_w octaves, rattle_rate\ncollisions/s, rattle_decay s.\n\nChosen BY EAR (2026-09-28) from five fitted takes: this is \"H4 — tight\"\n(rattle_decay 0.058 -\u003e 0.042, env_tail 28 -\u003e 36); the looser takes were\njudged \"too low pitched\". The fit's best-scoring take (4.1) was the looser\nH1; the ear preferred the tighter chick.\n\nShared by hihat, hihat-lofi and hihat-pedal (each keeps its own DefaultFX).",
